# Local dev environment overrides.
#
# Copy this file to `dev.env` (git-ignored) and uncomment/edit what you want to change.
# It is sourced by the Makefile, by several others script in hack/ folder and by the devcontainer shell
# So it applies identically on the host and inside the devcontainer. Use simple, unquoted values.
#

# Image registry used by `make docker-push` and `make charts`.
# Override to build and push dev images under your own registry.
# Main official repository is quay.io/kubocd
# Setting this value here or in your environment is required
#
#REGISTRY=quay.io/your-user


# Other settings are optional. With no dev.env file, the defaults apply and
# the environment behaves exactly as if this file did not exist.

# Host port published for the local OCI registry (default: 5001). Change it if
# 5001 is already in use on your machine. NOTE: if the registry is already
# running, run `make dev-down` before `make dev-up` for the new port to apply.
#
#KUBOCD_REGISTRY_PORT=5001


# When running Kubocd locally (`make run`), a local Helm repository server is set up.
# Binding address may be changed if conflicting with pre-existing service
#
# HELM_REPO_ADV_ADDR="localhost:9090"
